[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Edgemodders/REDnode/main/packs/sound-tools/nexus/brand/banner.png[/img][/center]

[center][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Hear what Night City plays. Find any of its sounds. Swap in your own while the game runs.[/color][/b][/size][/center]

[center][size=3]REDnode Sound Tools is an app pack for sound modders: three windows over the game that show every sound Cyberpunk 2077 plays as it plays it, search all of its sound events, play any recording on the spot, and swap a sound mod into the running game without a restart.[/size][/center]

[line]

[quote][size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]STATUS: PREVIEW[/color][/b][/size]
Built in the open and tested in the game on game version 2.31; 0.1.1 is for game 2.5, where sound swaps and Sound Tracer are untested so far. It runs on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url], which you need first.
[b]Sound modders:[/b] this is for you. [b]Players:[/b] you do not need it to play sound mods.[/quote][line]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35537/35537-1792510038-529163682.png[/img]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]What is in the pack[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Sound Tracer[/color][/b][/size]
Start a trace and play. [b]Played[/b] lists every sound event the game sends to its audio engine, live, with its name and id. [b]Loaded[/b] lists every sound the game loads, by its sound id.
[list]
[*][b]Play[/b] on a Played row plays that event's own recordings, one variation each press, so you hear it even when it happened across the street. [b]G[/b] posts it through the game instead, with the game's own mix.[/*]
[*][b]Play[/b] on a Loaded row plays that one recording, exactly as it sits in the game's files.[/*]
[*]Filter, pause, copy any name or id, Stop and Stop all.[/*]
[*]A box that plays whatever you paste: an event name, an event id or a sound id.[/*]
[*]Every row is also written to [i]red4ext/logs/rednode-sound-trace.log[/i], so nothing is lost when the list scrolls on.[/*]
[/list][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35537/35537-1792523382-1774960424.png[/img]


[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Sound Search[/color][/b][/size]
Search the game's 20,569 sound events by name, event id or sound id. Each result shows the event's recordings: play the event, or one recording on its own. Save what you find to the [b]Scratch[/b] tab to come back to later; it is kept between game sessions.
Names come from WolvenKit's list of the game's events (through REDbridge); events newer than that list show as ids. Recordings come from the game's own sound index, so a sound you swapped in shows up as soon as it is in the game.

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35537/35537-1792510518-130940620.png[/img]

[size=4][b][color=#19f3ff]Hot swap[/color][/b][/size]
Swap an archive into the running game: type its name or path, press Swap, and the game loads it. That includes sound mods: REDnode pauses the game for a moment, holds its audio, loads the game's sound index again and lets it go, so your new sounds play without a restart.
[b]One limit:[/b] a sound that played just before the swap can keep its old version until the game loads it again (for a weapon, equip it again).

[img width=474]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/3333/images/35537/35537-1792523268-1183143616.png[/img]

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]A sound modding loop[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Trace: do the thing in the game (draw the katana) and read its event in the Tracer.[/*]
[*]Search: open that event in Sound Search and play its recordings to find the one you want.[/*]
[*]Make your version, for example with [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/EDGEwave]EDGEwave[/url], and pack it as an archive.[/*]
[*]Hot swap: swap the archive in and hear it in the game, without leaving it.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url] 0.41.0 or later, with what it needs (RED4ext, redscript).[/*]
[*]Nothing more for Hot swap: it swaps through [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/36172]REDswap[/url], which REDnode 0.41.0 installs. (Pack 0.1.0, for game 2.31, needs RED Hot Tools 1.3 or later.)[/*]
[*]Optional: REDbridge, for event names. Without it, events show as ids. REDnode's Mod Manager has a [b]Get REDbridge[/b] button that installs it, with no admin rights.[/*]
[*]Cyberpunk 2077 on PC, game version 2.5. For game 2.31, use pack 0.1.0 with REDnode 0.37.0. On a game version REDnode does not know, sound swaps are refused.[/*]
[/list][size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Install[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] Mod Manager Download, then enable and deploy.[/*]
[*][b]By hand:[/b] extract the zip into the game folder, so the apps land in [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode/apps/[/i].[/*]
[/list]In the game, press [b]F10[/b] and open the [b]Mod Manager[/b] from the launcher (the [b]REDNODE[/b] tab at the lower left). Switch on the apps you want; they start switched off. Hot swap asks to change the game's archives: allow it there.

[b]Uninstall:[/b] remove it in your mod manager, or delete the three app folders ([i]sound-tracer[/i], [i]sound-search[/i], [i]hot-swap[/i]) from [i]red4ext/plugins/REDnode/apps/[/i]. REDnode itself stays.

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]For mod makers[/color][/b][/size]

Everything these apps do is in REDnode's [b]rednode[/b] package, for your own mods: [i]audio.trace[/i] for the live list, [i]audio.playGame[/i] to play a game sound or an event's recordings, [i]audio.eventSounds[/i] for an event's recordings, [i]audio.event[/i] to post an event through the game, and [i]archives.reload[/i] to swap archives. See the [url=https://edgemodders.github.io/REDnode/sound.html]Sound API docs[/url].

[size=5][b][color=#fcee0a]Questions[/color][/b][/size]

[b]Why is Play on some events greyed out?[/b]
Some events have no recordings of their own: stop events (names ending in [i]_stop[/i]) only stop another sound, and some events play sound that lives elsewhere in the game. Hover the button for the reason. [b]G[/b] still posts them through the game.

[b]Why does G sometimes play nothing?[/b]
G posts the event on V. Many sounds belong to something else in the world (an NPC's footsteps, a car) and need its state, such as the ground under it. Play, which plays the recordings themselves, always works when the event has any.

[b]Does tracing slow the game down?[/b]
No cost showed in the tests. The first trace of a session takes a fraction of a second to start while REDnode finds the game's sound tables.

[b]Is it free?[/b]
Yes, and open source under the MIT license, in [url=https://github.com/Edgemodders/REDnode]REDnode's repo[/url].

